      "id": "a1-u03-d06-t01",
      "before": "a1-u03-d06-e01",
      "title": { "en": "Twój and twoja" },
      "body": { "en": "\"Your\", to a friend you call *ty*, works like *mój* and *moja*: *twój brat*, *twoja siostra*. To several people, or to someone you call *pan* or *pani*, Polish uses other words, which come in a later Unit." }
    },
    {
      "id": "a1-u03-d06-t02",
      "before": "a1-u03-d06-e05",
      "title": { "en": "Syn, córka, mąż, żona" },
      "body": { "en": "The endings tell you the gender. *Syn* and *mąż* end in a consonant: *mój syn*, *mój mąż*. *Córka* and *żona* end in *-a*: *moja córka*, *moja żona*. To ask an age: *ile lat ma twój syn?*" }
    }
  ],
